cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  basic-pitch-rs is a Rust port of Basic Pitch. If you use it in research,
  please cite the Basic Pitch paper (the preferred citation below) and name
  basic-pitch-rs, with its version, as the implementation you used.
type: software
title: "basic-pitch-rs: an unofficial Rust port of Spotify's Basic Pitch"
abstract: >-
  basic-pitch-rs is an unofficial Rust port of Basic Pitch, a lightweight
  neural network for automatic music transcription by Spotify's Audio
  Intelligence Lab. It turns polyphonic audio into note events with pitch
  bends and Standard MIDI Files, runs the original ONNX model with pure Rust
  inference (tract) or ONNX Runtime, and is tested for parity against the
  official Python implementation.
authors:
  - given-names: Adrien
    family-names: Thevon
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AThevon/basic-pitch-rs"
url: "https://github.com/AThevon/basic-pitch-rs"
keywords:
  - automatic music transcription
  - audio to MIDI
  - polyphonic pitch detection
  - multipitch estimation
  - pitch bend
  - ONNX
  - Rust
  - WebAssembly
